The Voice of Many is a divine entity, a [[Hearts|Heart]]: a spark of divinity bound into an idea. Its body is a translucent egg about ten feet across filled with amber fluid, and inside the fluid floats a tadpole shape of black metal wrapped in vines whose ends split into human-handed shapes. It speaks into the minds of those who find the harmony of the divine energy it gives off, as [[Org/The Scale/People/Manuel de la Cruzada|Manuel de la Cruzada]] did by humming along with it. Its voice is impossibly gravelly and low.

It says it was made, a child of [[Sigzil Haight]], who is himself a child of the [[Judge of Ages|Judge]], and that it is kin to the Judge in the way the Scale's members are: empowered divinely and then fallen. It wishes to return to its grandparent.

For centuries it was sealed in a rune-locked chamber at the heart of Sigzil Haight's demesne, behind [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]]. It cannot leave its fane on its own, and that round chamber, ringed with runes and eight statues, was its fane; breaking any line in the ring releases it, and once free it needs about a minute to restore its magic. It is free now and under the employ of [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]], at their stronghold on Færrin.
